>> title: Honey Dijon Pork Tenderloin
>> servings: 8
>> source: https://belleofthekitchen.com/honey-dijon-pork-tenderloin/

Preheat oven to 350. Place the @pork tenderloin{1%package} into a #steel high-walled sautee pan{}. 

In a small bowl, whisk together the @soy sauce{0.25%cup}, @honey{3%tbsp}, @olive oil{3%tbsp}, @orange juice{2%tbsp}, @dijon mustard{2%tbsp}, @garlic{3-4%cloves}(minced), @dried rosemary{2%teaspoons}(or 1 sprig freshly chopped), and @black pepper{} to taste. 

Cut small slits in the top of each of the tenderloin with a #paring knife{}, about halfway through (about 6 slits on each). Pour the sauce over the top. 

Bake in the preheated oven for ~{40-50%minutes}, spooning the sauce over the top of the tenderloins every ~{10%minutes}. This creates a glaze on top, and will soak into the slits you cut in the meat. Bake until a #meat thermometer{} inserted in the largest part of the tenderloins reads 145F.

Remove tenderloin from the oven and allow to rest for ~{10-15%minutes} before slicing and serving. Serve with sauce from the pan drizzled over the top. Enjoy!